      "writtenOn": "2024-03-14T00:07:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "right, i\u0027m suggesting the global `usb_mux_init` that is intended to be callable from\n\"anywhere\" do less work so it\u0027s thread safe - probably just manipulate the INIT flag.\nthen, when this flag is handled by the main mux code, the real work can happen.\nthese operations probably get serialized fine when when the mux task isn\u0027t\nenabled, but with all the mux operations handled by the mux task, i think we\u0027ll\nrun into issues if another task can directly init the mux.",
      "parentUuid": "76246f82_f94febdf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 487,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 487,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "8af423bae40ae13ce5b1b52c91fc58c52309095b",
