        "id": 1527433
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-15T21:40:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think even clearing the INIT flag could cause some issues. For example, if the USB mux task was running `perform_mux_set` it may initialize the mux, then later run `exit_low_power_mode`. That will return an error if the INIT flag is not set. So, another task clearing the INIT flag between the `usb_mux_init` call and `exit_low_power_mode` call in `perform_mux_set` would prevent the driver from configuring the mux.\n\nWhat about the fix in PS2? This structures mux initialization similar to mux setting. There is a `perform_*` function which actually initializes the mux. All the calls in usb_mux.c use `perform_mux_init`. And the global `usb_mux_*` will que the event instead of directly calling it when the mux task is enabled.",
      "parentUuid": "960168d9_233f35c7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 487,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 487,
        "endChar": 43
      },
